comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T07:12:45.389Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate-check evidence (all-status pm search over SDK surface, entrypoint, subpath, exports, tiering, import cost): matched closed pm-xzhz, pm-rjqr, pm-ju83, pm-ds3b, pm-9x6e, pm-8778, pm-79fr, pm-16ue and open pm-usfg, pm-e6tm5c, pm-92if. The closed set is promotion work (moving capability INTO the SDK) and boundary work (stopping private-core imports OUT of CLI/MCP); pm-e6tm5c is the snapshot/change gate over whatever shape exists. Nothing owns the partitioning of the surface or its import cost. Filed as a child of pm-usfg."
  "2026-07-25T07:12:46.141Z","harness:claude-code","Surface measurement: Object.keys on the published sdk entry yields 881 exports (693 functions, 188 values). src/sdk/index.ts is 35 'export *' lines, so any new module file joins the public surface with no review step. package.json exports declares four subpaths only ('.', './sdk', './sdk/runtime', './sdk/testing'); dist/sdk/index.d.ts carries 102 top-level export statements. Import cost measured against a 41ms bare-node baseline: sdk.js 289ms, main.js 286ms — importing one SDK primitive costs the same as launching the whole CLI. Contract constants (ACTIVITY_COMMANDER_STRING_OPTION_CONTRACTS, CALENDAR_FLAG_CONTRACTS, CONTEXT_FLAG_CONTRACTS and siblings) sit in the same namespace as authoring primitives with no marker distinguishing them."
  "2026-07-25T11:31:40.354Z","harness:codex","Evidence: aggregate SDK compatibility is preserved while eight capability subpaths are independently importable in packed Node and Bun consumers. All linked import/type/surface tests passed; the clean import-cost rerun verified all 10 entrypoints within committed budgets."
